	"draftqueens": ["Time to draw. I'm tossing three cards and keeping two queens, and honestly, Rico, you're the next thing getting tossed.", "Last draw, sweetie. I'm discarding my manners and keeping the queens.", "One draw, sweetie. That's one more chance than your life ever gave you.", "I threw away three cards and kept two queens. Try that with your friends, Rico. Oh wait, you'd have zero left.", "You're holding a pair of twos and a lot of hope. Only one of those ever pays, and it's not the hope.", "Ow! Not the face, I just redrew it!", "Hey! That was my good card!", "Five cards, one draw, and you drew a gravestone.", "Nice try, sweetie. I drew a queen, and you drew the dirt."],
	"fandool": ["Fifth street, baby! Every card you hold is face up, so the whole room gets to watch you panic.", "Seventh street, the last card, face down! It's my only secret, and it's an ace.", "In stud your up cards are face up, Rico. Everyone can see your hand, even the people who left.", "There's nowhere to hide in stud, and nowhere to run either. It's a package deal.", "A seven and a three showing on fourth street? That's bringing a spork to a gunfight.", "Foul! Somebody review the tape!", "Ref! He hit me! Ref! ...I'm the ref. Ow.", "And that's the game, folks! Me winning, you losing, and a nice highlight for the replay.", "Replay that in slow motion. I want to watch you fall in high definition."],
	"pokerstarz": ["Chat, he's actually good! Smash that like button while I destroy him for the clip!", "New strategy: I'm using all four hole cards. That's illegal in Omaha, but I have sponsors.", "Omaha says use exactly two hole cards, Rico. You're using zero, because you're holding a pair of excuses.", "Chat, he's got four hole cards and still found a way to have nothing. That's content.", "Like, subscribe, and fold, in that order. Then consider a career change, like therapy.", "Hey! No hitting on stream!", "Ow! I'm getting demonetized!", "And that's the clip: 'Idiot Loses Everything With Four Hole Cards.' Thumbnail is your face.", "GG, no re. You're going on my highlight reel, right next to my other victims. Also you."],
	"betmgn": ["Three cards isn't simple once you see the ante. That's my fee for existing.", "Final hand, Rico. Three cards, one ante, and my commission scales with your screaming.", "Three-card poker is easy. You get three cards, I get your money, and the math is very consistent.", "Pair Plus pays when you have a pair, Rico. You've never had a pair of anything but problems.", "Ante up everything you own, and I'll let you keep your three cards. They're yours, and they're bad.", "Ow! That's coming out of your payout!", "Three cards, not three hits!", "Three cards, three seconds. That's efficiency with a healthy margin.", "Pair Plus pays on a pair. You just paid plus. Thanks for playing."],
	"steake": ["You hurt me, but in Razz the worst hand wins, so I'm technically ahead. To the moon!", "All in on the dip! In Razz the best hand is ace to five, and mine is a panic attack.", "In Razz the lowest hand wins, so you're finally a natural. Congratulations on your entire career.", "King, queen, jack showing? In Razz that's a disaster, and in life it's just your usual Tuesday.", "I've got diamond hands, Rico, mostly because the real ones got liquidated.", "Dip! Buy the dip! ...Oh no, I'm the dip.", "Rug pull! And I don't even own a rug!", "You've been liquidated, buddy. Unlike your portfolio, I'm thrilled about it.", "Not financial advice, but I'm taking your wallet and your dignity. Mostly the dignity."],
	"bovadoh": ["Impressive. Now I will play both hands at once, which is easy, since neither has ever been challenged.", "I have two hands and you have one. Soon you will have none, which is a metaphor and also a threat.", "Seven cards, split into five and two. Both hands are better than your life, and I'm including the childhood.", "You keep arranging your hands, Rico, as if there's a version where you win. Charming, like watching a dog drive.", "In Pai Gow, ties go to the banker, and I am the banker. So your best case is losing slowly.", "Hm. That stung. I'll cry about it later, at a spa.", "Do that again, and I will pretend not to notice. Twice.", "Both of my hands won, and both of yours were mostly regret.", "I'll file this under Tuesday, like everything else I have beaten."],
	"seezers": ["You have wounded Caesar, so I shall hit on sixteen. I fear nothing, not even math.", "Seventeen, and I STAND. You, however, will fall like Rome, only faster and with less paperwork.", "The dealer hits sixteen and stands on seventeen. It's Rome's rule for conquering, with more stabbing.", "You split your eights? A thing split is a thing broken, and I say that as a man stabbed twenty-three times.", "Want to double down, Rico? You already doubled your debt. Why not take insurance on your life?", "By Juno! That was my good toga!", "Et tu, Rico?! Et twenty-two, I bust!", "Veni, vidi, bust. And by 'bust' I mean you hit on twelve, and now you're a statue.", "Hail, Caesar. The dealer wins, and the player becomes a footnote."],
	"wynners": ["A natural eight? How adorable. I have a natural too, and mine comes with a wine cellar.", "Banker, Player, or Tie. Bet on any of them, Rico, but mercy is not on the table.", "In baccarat the player decides nothing. I find that peaceful. In your case, accurate.", "A tie pays eight to one, and it appears about as often as my affection for you.", "Squeeze the cards slowly, darling. It's tradition, and the only time you'll hold on to anything.", "How rude. I have not been struck since finishing school.", "Mon Dieu, you have bled on the baize. It's imported.", "The Banker wins, as ever, and the Player, as ever, is you, on the floor.", "Adieu, darling. You'd have made an excellent tie. That pays eight to one, but not to you."],
	"snake_eyes": ["Come out roll! Seven or eleven, I win. Anything else, I blame you.", "Point's set, Rico. Hit your number before a seven, or die. Mostly die.", "Seven or eleven on the come out, you lose. I've decided that applies to your actual life too.", "Snake eyes is two ones, Rico. That's exactly how many friends you have, and I'm counting me.", "Roll a seven after your point and you lose. So naturally, that's the one number you'll love.", "Not the dice! They're my babies!", "Ow! Hit me, not my lucky dice!", "Seven out, pal. The shooter loses, and tonight the shooter is you.", "You never even rolled. The dice just looked at you and felt bad."],
