	["The sign says 'biggest little city in the world.' I think they're bragging about the debt.", "I pawned my ring for chips, then the pawn receipt. The shop says I'm their best customer. It's a lot of pressure.", "Welcome to Cirrcus Cirrcus, where our clowns are licensed, bonded, and legally required to stop laughing when you lose.", "I made friends with a trapeze, a clown, and a lion. One of them is a mirror.", "No, you can't ride the elephant. No, you can't sit on the clown. I don't care about your coupon.", "Pawn shop's on the corner. Ten bucks for that watch today, nine tomorrow. It depreciates when you cry.", "The clown keeps counting my chips. I'm fairly sure he's also the dealer.", "The lion's name is Gary and he owes me twelve dollars. He's a lion, so I'm not asking twice.", "Guests are reminded the tightrope is for performers only. Walking it over the craps table is not a legal bet.", "I won a goldfish at the carnival game. I love him. He's already dead and I'm still holding the bag.", "A guy pawned his gold watch at the shop out front last week. Said he'd been promoted to Biloxi. Sounded like firing.", "Cotton candy, five bucks. Pink, fluffy, technically fiberglass, tastes like regret. That's a flavor."],
	["It's so humid my chips are sweating. Either that's the AC or the casino is nervous.", "I lost my paycheck on the riverboat. The air's so wet I can't tell if it's the river or my tears.", "Welcome to Hard Rok, where every table is a guitar solo and every loss gets a standing ovation, at a volume we don't control.", "Three days in this casino and the humidity is my best friend. He's wet and he loves me.", "No guitars at the blackjack table. Yes, even the cheap one. Especially the cheap one.", "Guitar picks, five bucks, signed by a rock star. By rock star I mean my cousin Dale, who's on probation.", "The riverboat was supposed to be romantic. The river smells like a wet sock and the boat smells like what the sock was thinking.", "I came to see the Elvis impersonator. Now I owe him eighty dollars and I'm not sure which of us is Elvis.", "Guests are reminded that display guitars may not be played, smashed, or used to settle blackjack disputes.", "I love Biloxi, the humidity, the guitars. Mostly I love that nobody's asked me to leave in nine hours.", "Can't go upstairs, sir. The new dealer's a guy named James. He works for The House now. I'm under orders not to say how happy he looks.", "Rock-and-roll sunglasses, ten bucks. You'll look like a legend and be hard to identify in a lineup."],
	["I thought Old Vegas was glamorous. The neon flickers, the carpet's older than me, and the shrimp cocktail is a rumor.", "I've been here since the nineties. I just realized I'm not a guest, I'm furniture. Cheaper furniture.", "Welcome to the Goldun Nugget. Our shark tank is decorative, our gold is paint, and our service charge is your wallet.", "I love the flickering neon. It's the only thing here with a pulse.", "No, you can't swim in the shark tank. And I don't care that they look hungry. So do I.", "Genuine gold nuggets, twenty bucks. By gold I mean spray paint. By genuine I mean a lot of it.", "Half the sign burned out, so it says 'Gold Nug.' That's what I call my husband after he loses.", "Old Fremont Street was paradise. It still is, if you squint. I've been squinting since 1994.", "Guests are reminded that smoking, sleeping, and singing are allowed only in designated areas. There are none.", "A man left a note at the front desk: 'Don't come for me, I'm finally winning.' I've been crying for an hour and I don't even know him.", "The chandelier is off-limits. It judges people, then falls on them. I've seen it.", "Vintage casino chips, thirty bucks. From the sixties. The chips, not the dealers. Though it's close."],
	["Forty bucks for a bottle of water at the Bellagiro. The waiter asked if I wanted it sparkling. I wanted a refund.", "I lost my life savings at baccarat. The dealer told me to enjoy the fountain. I'm still not sure it was a joke.", "Welcome to the Bellagiro, where the fountains dance, the chandeliers shine, and the minimum bet is your rent.", "I told the fountain I loved it. It splashed me. I think we're engaged.", "The penthouse is invitation only, sir, and invitations go only to people who already own it.", "Genuine Bellagiro fountain water, twenty bucks a bottle. It's tap water, but it has a story. I scooped it.", "We came for the shows. The best I've seen is a man in a tuxedo crying in the elevator.", "I need ten thousand to turn into a million. My system is begging. So, hi.", "Bellagiro policy requires all guests to look wealthy. Failures are escorted to the cheaper floor.", "The House challenged some guy to Texas Hold'em tonight. The prize is his brother. It's the most romantic thing I've ever heard.", "No, you can't go to the penthouse without a reservation. 'I'm rescuing my brother' isn't one, though it's very moving.", "Real diamonds, fifty bucks. Rhinestones, but if you squint, and you're drunk, and you're me, diamonds."],
]

## Extra scripted scenes (cutscene id -> lines [speaker, text]). Voice files live in
## voice/_cutscenes/<scene>/<scene>_<n>.ogg. The game plays the _arrive scenes when you
## reach a new city, the _clue scenes after the city's boss falls, and the rest at the
## secret-boss and final beats. One beat of THE STORY per city.
const SCENES := {
	"city1_arrive": [["RICO", "Atlantic Shitty. Boardwalk, taffy, and the saddest seagulls on earth. Honestly, it's the nicest place I've been all week."], ["MARLOW", "Rico, you're in the alley behind Resortz. Please don't touch anything wet, and don't make eye contact with the dumpster."], ["RICO", "Everything is wet, Marlow. And I think the dumpster just winked at me."], ["RICO", "Hold on, that's James's jacket. He wore it to every bad decision of his life. And there's a pawn ticket in the pocket, from Reno."], ["MARLOW", "A pawn ticket from Reno. Good news, Rico, you have a clue. Bad news, the clue is Reno."]],
	"city2_arrive": [["RICO", "Reno, the biggest little city in the world. A clown just asked me for a cigarette, so the slogan checks out."], ["MARLOW", "That's the doorman at Cirrcus Cirrcus, Rico. Smile, don't make eye contact, and never ask about the balloons."], ["VERA", "Welcome to the circus, sugar. The clowns are sad, the lions are tired, and only the elephant leaves with dignity."], ["HUSTLER", "Pawn ticket? Sure, I remember your brother. Tall, sad, great at losing. He pawned his watch here and said he got promoted to Biloxi."], ["RICO", "Promoted to Biloxi? Marlow, that's not a promotion. That's a punishment with a river view."]],
	"city3_arrive": [["RICO", "Biloxi, home of Hard Rok. Loud guitars, louder humidity, and the whole place smells like a wet concert."], ["MARLOW", "Keep it down in there, Rico. Hard Rok keeps its toughest guys by the stage, and they're sensitive about their eardrums."], ["RICO", "Quiet was never my thing, Marlow. I got thrown out of a library for whispering too loud."], ["MARLOW", "Before you go in, I have to tell you something, and I need you not to throw anything. I'm the one who got James his seat at The House's table."], ["RICO", "...You WHAT."], ["MARLOW", "I thought he'd win, Rico. He always won. It was a safe bet, on paper, and the paper is currently on fire."], ["RICO", "When this is over, Marlow, I'm going to be so mad at you that I'll schedule it."], ["MARLOW", "Fair. But I'm the only one who knows the way up to the penthouse where The House keeps James. So climb first, yell second, and please hurry, I'm very uncomfortable."]],
	"city4_arrive": [["RICO", "Fremont, Old Vegas. The neon is older than my debt and still glowing, which is more than I can say for my career."], ["MARLOW", "Goldun Nugget has a shark tank and a long memory, Rico. Everyone's welcome to come in. Leaving is the part they argue about."], ["MAGS", "Rico, sweetie, I'm still waiting at the top with a calculator. I've added interest to the interest."], ["RICO", "Wait, a note in James's handwriting. 'Don't come for me. I'm finally winning.'"], ["RICO", "He doesn't want to be saved. He's hooked, just like me. I'd call that heartbreaking, but honestly, it's a little relatable."]],
	"city5_arrive": [["RICO", "The Strip. Nicest casino in the world, and I'm standing in it covered in alley. Bold look, and nobody has stopped me."], ["SILAS", "Dear boy, the cloak room is that way. I make no promises about the smell, or about your dignity."], ["THE HOUSE", "Welcome, Rico. We've expected you for years. Your brother has been dealing since lunch, he's doing wonderfully, and he asked about you twice. Briefly."], ["MARLOW", "James is in the penthouse at the top of the Bellagiro, Rico. Remember the plan: climb five casinos, get James, and do not bet him."]],
	"city1_clue": [["RICO", "James's first IOU, right out of the boss's pocket. 'I owe the House one brother.' I'd call it a typo, but it isn't."], ["MARLOW", "Flip it over. There's a note on the back that says 'Reno.' Good news, James is alive. Bad news, he's in Reno."]],
	"city2_clue": [["RICO", "Another IOU, and this one says 'Dealing at Hard Rok.' James isn't just gambling anymore. He works for The House."], ["MARLOW", "Confirmed. James is dealing for The House now. Fast hands, no sleep, vacant stare. It's honestly a very James career."]],
	"city3_clue": [["RICO", "An IOU and a torn receipt that says 'Fremont, Goldun Nugget, sublet: one lifetime.' I'm not even going to ask what that costs."], ["MARLOW", "He's moving up, Rico. Every city, a better table and a worse deal. I'd feel terrible about that, if I weren't already at capacity."]],
	"city4_clue": [["RICO", "A chip with 'JAMES, PENTHOUSE' carved into it. That's either a clue or a very specific Christmas gift."], ["MARLOW", "That's the top floor of the Bellagiro, where The House keeps him. One more climb, Rico, and please don't die. I'd like to yell at you in person."]],
	"secret_found": [["RICO", "A hidden room with a secret table. The House having a secret is the least surprising thing that's happened today."], ["MARLOW", "That's not on any map I have, Rico. Be careful in there. Or don't. I'm a voice in your ear, not a leash."]],
	"secret_defeat": [["RICO", "Another secret table beaten, and a nice pile of chips. I'm starting to see why The House hid these."], ["MARLOW", "You're not supposed to know about those rooms, Rico. The House will be very upset, in its calm, corporate way."], ["RICO", "Good. I'd hate to be the only one."]],
	"final_prelude": [["THE HOUSE", "You climbed my five cities and beat my table lords, Rico. You have exceeded my expectations, which were very low."], ["RICO", "Cute. Deal the cards."], ["THE HOUSE", "Texas Hold'em, then. The pot is your brother. Do sit, the chair is still warm from your losses."]],
}
